  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DRG: PIDR Global Labor Program - Platform for Organizing by Workers for Empowerment and Recognition (GLP-POWER)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(USAID Bureau for Development, Democracy, and Innovation (D):  The Global Labor Program - Platform for Organizing by Workers for Empowerment and Recognition (GLP-POWER)  is implemented by a coalition of global, regional, and local organizations led by Solidar Suisse. GLP-POWER tests innovative means of organizing migrant and informal workers, who are particularly vulnerable to labor rights abuses and difficult to reach. These innovations include the use of technology (alongside in-person methods) to connect workers to each other, and to provide resources to assist them in protecting their rights. The project also conducts research in partnership with workers to put them in the lead in developing solutions to the challenges they face..With FY 2022 funds for Year-2 of the activity, GLP-POWER will build on the successful initial stages of development of the technology platform from Year-1, by adding additional modules, resources, and other types of content, and by socializing the platform among end-users while capturing feedback for continuous improvement. By doing so, vulnerable workers, and the organizations that represent and/or serve them, will be better able to access legal aid, migrants support, women&apos;s groups, and psychosocial services..GLP-POWER directly contributes to the Multilateral Partnership for Organizing, Worker Empowerment, and Rights (M-POWER) initiative, which is a key deliverable of the Presidential Initiative for Democratic Renewal (PIDR) that USAID collaborates on with the Department of Labor and U.S. Department of State&apos;s Bureau for Democracy, Rights, and Labor (DRL)..</narrative>
  </description>
